Labour plan to cut funds from heat pump scheme sparks industry backlash

@nestauk.bsky.social warned that cutting the BUS budget would send a “damaging signal” to business when heat pump installations were growing as a result of soaring gas prices in recent months
www.ft.com/content/e67...

Interest is growing

Aug 2026 saw highest-ever number of BUS heat-pump vouchers redeemed

@theCCCuk notes that "BUS continues to be the main driver of retrofit installations"

Heat pumps can also cut running costs

@OctopusEnergy says 99.6% of its Cosy heat pumps cost less to run than gas boilers, with customers using a smart tariff saving an average of £230 a year

Savings compared with oil heating can be higher

